omxplorer, a desktop data app (1440x900), importing a file: a centred dialog panel about 1100x760 over the dimmed, blurred app window. Header: title "Import sales-1m.parquet", under it "1,000,000 rows · 5 columns · read in 0.02 s" in green; on the right a 3-step progress control "File › Columns › Table" with Columns current. Then a preview grid of the first rows (columns order, amount, region, day, paid), each column header with a small type badge (#, 0.0, Aa, date, bool) and a tiny distribution histogram; about 9 rows; some empty amount cells. Then a "Columns" table, left-aligned, one row per column: name, a type dropdown (Integer, Decimal, Text, Date, Yes/No), Empty count (amber when non-zero: 49,912 and 30,283), Distinct values (5 for region), and the first values in grey. Footer: a quiet "Back" pill on the left, the primary "Create table" pill on the right with a table icon.
